{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/392889-necropoli-spectres","id":392889,"title":"Necropoli & Spectres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-04T12:34:46-08:00","id":392889,"title":"Necropoli & Spectres","content":"So I'm in the process of building a Necropolis for a game, and I was curious of everyone's thoughts on the Spectre-to-Wraith population. Much of the source material I've read seems to suggest that its rare for many Spectres to be able to reside so far away from the Tempest, resulting in just a few Dopplegangers at most to exist within an average Necropolis. Obviously there are exceptions in every case, but I'm wondering what the 'Wraith experts' thought was the most common occurances.<br /> <br /> My initial thought is about only 5% or so of the total wraith population would be secretly Spectres, as any more than that would risk discovery -- something they likely don't want unless their either more suicidal than an average Spectre, or just about ready to take down the whole town.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4938-shardsandwires","name":"shardsandwires","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T18:56:58-08:00","id":393302,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't have that many actual Spectres. I used Spectres in about the same percentage as there are criminals in a society - they are actually quite few, but have an outsized impact.<br /> <br /> I would, however, have a large population of Wraiths succumbing to Carthasis on a frequent or even regular basis allowing their Shadows to control them. They aren't Spectres yet, but when their Shadows are in control, they are unknowingly in contact with the few actual Spectres in the Necropolis or hiding in the nearby Tempest.<br /> <br /> I think that's even spookier than secret Spectres as some of the Wraiths betraying the Necropolis don't even know they are doing it. Spectres are just there to be destroyed. But Wraiths being controlled by their Shadows? There is a lot more to be done with that. A 5% population which is more controlled by their Shadows than Psyches is a good number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T03:37:17-08:00","id":393609,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I was going to reply with something, but Black Fox hit all the high points...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T11:27:43-08:00","id":393995,"title":"","content":"I agree with Naz and Black Fox. Last time I out-and-out designed a full-on Necropolis, I remember placing the VERY few Doppelgangers in specific places and I had most of them identified and knew who the others were roughly. I did have a few specters of other types at some VERY bad spots in town with significant Nihils. For example, there was one haunted house where a number of novice nun-nurses lived and the handyman came in and killed them with an axe (actual true story). The place was haunted by the specters of the killer and his victims but the axe-man was pretty much in complete control and they would all hide in the Tempest if they felt over-matched. But overall that was probably less than twenty &quot;resident&quot; specters in town, with the usual level of intrusion from the Tempest based on the current situation. <br /> <br /> As for wraiths in a specter-y way, one or so of the Legions (Silent, I think) ran a sort of &quot;sanity police&quot; trained to look for wraiths in Catharsis and get them to a Pardoner. (All the Legions had general policing duties, but, like a normal police department, there were special &quot;divisions&quot; or squads)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}